$$\begin{aligned}
& 6x + 3 + 1 = 5 \\
\Leftrightarrow & 6x + 4 = 5 \\
\Leftrightarrow & 6x = 1 \Leftrightarrow x = \frac{1}{6}
\end{aligned}$$
Vậy $x = \frac{1}{6}$.

$$\begin{aligned}
& (x^2 - 4) + x^2 - 3x + 15 = x^2 \\
\Leftrightarrow & 2x^2 - 3x + 11 = x^2 \\
\Leftrightarrow & -3x = -19 \Leftrightarrow x = \frac{19}{3}
\end{aligned}$$
Vậy $x = \frac{19}{3}$.
